WEBVTT

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:01.980
<b>Studio Hirroet</b>

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.600
<b>Rights Management Department</b>

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:05.890
C-Mizu!

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:09.020
How do you not know what our cash cow is?!

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:11.410
All of their scarves
are the same color!

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:14.830
It's a coincidence, I guess. The RGB 
values are all one number different...

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:16.820
Like hell it's a coincidence!

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:18.440
Are you stupid or what?!

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:21.990
If you have six siblings wearing <i>those </i>
colors, people will call it a rip-off!

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:24.330
You realize there's things you 
can't do in this business, right?!

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:25.540
Fujimoto

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:25.540
Scarf

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:25.540
Scarf

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:25.540
Belt 1

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:27.870
But they did it first, you know...

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:28.670
Fujimoto

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:29.410
Keep your mouth shut!

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.800
Part A

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:38.180
That's where we learned our lesson...

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:44.690
When we find a malicious work, we 
must purge it in a level-headed way.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:47.580
Isn't that right, C-Mizu-chan?

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:56.950
Rights Management 
Department

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:59.940
I'm sorry. He said no.

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.450
Yeah, I'm sorry.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:04.160
Understood.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:12.340
<b>Fujimoto</b>

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:12.340
As of this moment, we're to throw out 
the storyboards for episode five.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:13.410
What?!

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:15.840
<b>Four</b>

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:15.840
<b>Five</b>

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.840
<b>Six</b>

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:15.840
<b>Three</b>

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:15.840
<b>Two</b>

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:19.980
What the heck?

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:30.560
<b>Two</b>

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.840
We almost had it ready to air!

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:30.560
<b>Three</b>

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:29.270
<b>Four</b>

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.840
We have to start over from the storyboards?

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:29.270
<b>Five</b>

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:24.860
Why?

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:26.850
We'd been working on it in secret,

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:29.110
but someone in the company 
leaked it down the line.

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:30.560
<b>Six</b>

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:30.560
Oh, boy!

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:31.270
<b>Five</b>

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:31.900
Who was it?

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.480
Who would do something so foolish?

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.480
<b>Four</b>

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.480
<b>Fujimoto</b>

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:34.860
<b>Three</b>

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:34.860
<b>Fujimoto</b>

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:35.460
Seriously!

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.530
<b>Two</b>

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.520
They didn't get permission
to do it in the first place?

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:38.450
They didn't.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:45.330
<b>Three</b>

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:45.330
<b>Four</b>

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:45.330
<b>Six</b>

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:45.330
<b>Five</b>

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:45.330
<b>Two</b>

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:40.550
Why the hell not?!

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:45.320
Maybe the planning committee told themselves, 
"If someone else does it, it's okay for us."

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:48.130
You'd expect better
of grown-ups.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:48.040
<b>Four</b>

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:48.040
<b>Six</b>

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:48.040
<b>Fujimoto</b>

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:48.040
<b>Fujimoto</b>

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:50.070
What are we gonna do now?

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.080
<b>Five</b>

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:56.760
<b>Fujimoto</b>

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:54.740
The primary contractor studio has called in
 four fast-working "miracle storyboarders."

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:56.760
220,000? 
Give me a break...

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:54.590
Master, you're clearly
 teasing me.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:56.760
By morning? That's ridiculous.
I'll do it, though...

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:56.760
Rough draft? 
I don't do that crap.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:56.750
They started with just a plot outline,

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:59.350
and say they'll have composition 
and development in six hours.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:06.020
<b>Two</b>

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:06.020
<b>Three</b>

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:06.020
<b>Four</b>

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:06.020
<b>Five</b>

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:06.020
<b>Six</b>

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.200
That's ridiculous.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:04.870
For storyboards, splitting the A and B parts 
between two people should be the upper limit.

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:06.010
No kidding...

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:08.370
The decision can't be overturned.

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:09.800
Halt the current production.

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:11.270
Contact each member of the staff.

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:14.530
We're going to do our job right.

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:22.020
Yes... before <i>he</i> awakens.

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:29.750
<b>Hirroet Plus</b>

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:35.410
Yes. Understood.

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:38.490
They say the blue outlines have to go, too.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:14.980
<b>Magical Girl - On Vacation</b>

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:20.860
<b>Muscovado Curry</b>

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:20.860
<b>Souvenirs</b>

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:17.820
I love sata andagi!

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:20.860
<b>We're on a school trip!!</b>

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:19.700
Yeah, so good!

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:23.360
<b>The Destruction of Sagami-OHno</b>

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:28.940
<i>An enormous creature has arisen out of 
MiyagaSAY Lake in Kanagawa Prefecture.</i>

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:30.380
<i>Its name: Chizilla.</i>

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:32.450
<i>It came ashore and started 
heading northeast.</i>

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:36.420
<i>When it reached Sagami-OHno, it discharged 
its incredibly destructive lasers,</i>

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:38.070
<i>and destroyed the entire city.</i>

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:44.430
<b>Tama River Final Defense Line</b>

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:41.440
<i>The enormous creature then 
continued northeast.</i>

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:44.070
<i>To keep it from reaching Tokyo, 
the government formed</i>

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:46.180
<i>a last line of defense at the Tama River,</i>

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:47.470
<i>and executed Operation: Tama.</i>

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:50.440
<i>They unleashed considerable firepower 
against the giant creature.</i>

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:54.530
<i>As a result, its advance was 
halted near Minami-Tama.</i>

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:57.940
<b>Episode Five Cut Revision 
Planning Headquarters</b>

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:00.860
But why would the enormous 
creature start heading northeast,

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.960
<b>Sagami-OHno</b>

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:01.170
<b>Karakida</b>

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:02.190
<b>Tama City</b>

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:04.490
fire off its lasers, then 
move on to Minami-Tama?

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:02.190
<b>Koremasa Bridge</b>

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:05.030
<b>Two</b>

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:07.200
<b>Three</b>

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:07.190
Because it was hungry, maybe?

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:09.090
Any word from the primary contractor?

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:17.370
<b>Two</b>

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:11.350
The storyboards should be ready in one hour.

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:13.440
The director checks can 
happen while we work here.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:17.370
Of course, given the situation, touching up 
dialogue will be about all we can do...

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:20.570
The situation? You mean the city 
being a hellscape and all?

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:23.550
The other stations will be going 
full "clip show" all day.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:26.580
And the other civilians 
have already evacuated.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.990
We need to stay here until the 
episode is ready to hand in.

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:31.560
That was the decision of 
the planning committee.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:32.930
Geh! Slavedrivers!

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:34.770
<b>Five</b>

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:34.770
<b>Fujimoto</b>

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:34.760
What's taking the primary contractor so long?

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:34.770
<b>Six</b>

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:37.770
I hear the upcoming episode 
is really taxing.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:37.770
<b>Fujimoto</b>

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:37.770
<b>Six</b>

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:37.770
<b>Four</b>

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:37.770
<b>Two</b>

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:37.770
<b>Three</b>

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:37.770
<b>Five</b>

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.210
<b>Alas...</b>

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.740
Well, given the situation, we'll 
have to let the primary contractor

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:43.370
take the lead on the episode 
while we support them.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.350
<b>Hoping for ??</b>

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:43.350
<b>Negotiating deadline</b>

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:45.080
We're getting new funding in.

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:47.180
It's quite a significant amount, too.

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:49.950
Due to the maintenance 
our cyborg bodies require,

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:52.500
it's hard to get by on the funding we have.

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:55.880
That's why we have to take this job.

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:58.210
Sounds like something Doc 
would jump at, of course...

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:00.430
I see.

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:02.110
Well, for the primary contractor,

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:05.170
it means even if the episode sucks, 
they can put the blame on us, right?

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:06.160
Precisely!

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:08.460
Was it the production 
controller that contacted you?

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:16.430
<b>Fujimoto</b>

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:16.430
<b>Six</b>

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:16.430
<b>Four</b>

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:16.430
<b>Two</b>

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:16.430
<b>Three</b>

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:16.430
<b>Five</b>

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:10.880
No, the supervising producer.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:14.670
Haven't heard much from Chiba-san 
at the desk lately. I hope he's okay.

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:15.410
You don't think...

00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:16.430
He skipped out?

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:21.430
Not funny...

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:23.440
<b>18 Hours Ago</b>

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:32.160
<b>Massive Creature Disaster Planning Headquarters
Special Briefing Room</b>

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:27.920
This is the data on the tissue sample 
retrieved from the giant creature.

00:06:28.460 --> 00:06:32.140
We've confirmed human DNA in its blood.

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:34.030
Human DNA?

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:36.480
We've performed an analysis on the DNA.

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:39.580
By strange coincidence, it's a 
match for a Japanese citizen.

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:43.990
He works as a production controller for 
an animation studio in Suginami.

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:43.990
32 Years Old 
Blood Type AB

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:46.240
Call him here at once.

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:50.920
His medical history may lead us to a virus 
that could affect the massive creature.

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:52.870
No, that's not possible.

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:53.840
Why not?

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:57.800
He's been missing for the past three days.

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:02.310
<b>MiyagaSAY Lake Parking Lot</b>

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:04.460
We've found a company car in the MiyageSAY 
Lake parking lot that we believe he left behind.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:06.890
Anything inside?

00:07:06.890 --> 00:07:09.730
A few finished keyframes for 
a show that's airing soon.

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:11.210
And this note.

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:14.860
"You've put out the orders you wanted.

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:18.800
I'll do the same. 
Then you can collect as you want."

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:20.580
It doesn't make much sense, does it?

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.460
Show me the keyframes you found.

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:28.130
This is awful. People get paid for this?

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:29.850
Goodness me...

00:07:29.850 --> 00:07:32.510
This is the dark underbelly of Japanimation.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:34.740
You think the finished 
cuts drove him to despair,

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:36.390
and he threw himself into MiyagaSAY Lake,

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:41.010
where his genetic material miraculously 
fused with that of a mysterious creature there?

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:45.390
32 Years Old 
Blood Type AB

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:44.540
No, he didn't necessarily throw himself in.

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:45.400
Look at this.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:48.350
He seemed to be playing a certain 
mobile game while walking.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:53.110
About three days ago, people were 
talking on social media about how you could

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:55.290
catch a rare monster near MiyagaSAY Lake.

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:59.480
So after picking up the key frames, he 
stopped here and met a tragic fate.

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:08.530
If only they'd put up signs prohibiting 
smartphone use while walking sooner.

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:10.130
<b>Episode Five Cut Revision Strategic Headquarters</b>

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:10.130
<b>-5RS-</b>

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:14.640
Enormous Creature Named "Chizilla"

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:15.360
The government has officially given the 
giant monster the name of "Chizilla."

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:16.810
Chizilla time!

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:17.750
Lame.

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:20.460
That's a foolproof way to get 
people to stop calling it that.

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:21.140
<b>Five</b>

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:24.510
You gotta be kidding!

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:27.960
This is a map of Chizilla's 
movements so far!

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:26.610
<b>Two</b>

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:26.610
<b>Six</b>

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:26.610
<b>Three</b>

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:26.610
<b>Four</b>

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:26.610
<b>Five</b>

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:29.320
<b>Sagami-OHno</b>

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:32.110
If we match it to the notes Chiba-san left 
behind about picking up the keyframes...

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:30.650
<b>Minami-Tama</b>

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:32.610
<b>Suginami</b>

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:33.950
<b>Two</b>

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:35.990
<b>Three</b>

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:35.990
<b>Four</b>

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:34.960
They're the same!

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:35.990
So what?

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.740
<b>Two</b>

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.740
<b>Six</b>

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.740
<b>Three</b>

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.740
<b>Four</b>

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.740
<b>Five</b>

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:38.350
Dunno...

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:44.310
It lines up perfectly with 
the information we have.

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:50.890
The massive organism Chizilla seems to be 
matching the movements of the missing Mr. Chiba.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:54.250
Is that even possible?

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:55.510
There's no precedent.

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:57.020
Who made that claim?

00:08:57.010 --> 00:09:01.670
32 Years Old 
Blood Type AB

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:58.990
This is my conclusion.

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:01.670
This will be Chizilla's final destination.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:15.650
<b>Suginami</b>

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:03.540
Suginami?

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:05.000
But why there, of all places?

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:06.490
Don't they usually attack big cities?

00:09:06.490 --> 00:09:10.450
Giant monsters usually prefer to 
destroy famous landmarks, don't they?

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:12.720
Either it's Mr. Chiba's intent
to bring back the keyframes,

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:15.650
or perhaps a homing instinct 
sending him there.

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:19.910
You're saying he's going back 
to the studio where he works?

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:21.630
It's commendable, in a sense.

00:09:21.630 --> 00:09:23.690
A true hero of the anime industry.

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:26.840
Well, as long as he's not coming 
here, that's one silver lining.

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:29.130
Don't say that in front of 
the press. You'll get fired.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:30.840
Yeah, right. I'm not that stupid.

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:35.570
If Suginami is attacked, it will put a stop 
to almost all Japanese anime production.

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:36.840
It will be a severe blow.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:40.990
Surely there are studios making 
anime outside of Suginami?

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:45.530
Very little Japanese anime 
is made 100% in-house.

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:48.700
Outsourcing to other production 
companies is the norm these days.

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:51.690
Suginami contains numerous 
anime affiliate companies.

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:56.690
Not just colorists, but compositing, 
editing, and many other departments.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:00.740
Animation Studio Distribution Rates

00:09:57.040 --> 00:10:00.500
Combined with its neighbor, Nerima, it's over 70%.

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:00.740
Suginami

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:00.740
Nerima

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:00.740
Other

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:04.360
If Suginami meets the same
 fate as Sagami-OHno,

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:06.250
our anime industry will...

00:10:07.110 --> 00:10:08.240
It will... what?

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:11.250
It may end... forever.

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:13.400
I won't get to see how 
my favorite anime ends?!

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:16.310
I won't get to hear voice actress
Hego-chan's voice anymore?!

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:18.730
It was supposed to have a 
second cour! Screw that!

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:20.890
<b>The End of the Anime Industry</b>

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:22.160
They finally confirmed a movie 
after that crowdfunding campaign!

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:23.830
I already put down a deposit for the DVD!

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:28.260
It's informal, but we received a response 
from the location in question.

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:30.560
"Protect Suginami.

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:33.660
Don't cancel anime forever."

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:34.680
What?

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:36.110
Don't let it reach Suginami!

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:35.770
So they're getting involved?

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:40.800
Animators can manage with pencil and paper, 
but the other divisions can't work without a PC!

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:38.870
At least evacuate the anime staff just in case!

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:38.030
This is bad in so many ways...

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:40.990
<b>The End of the Anime Industry</b>

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:43.320
If they evacuate now, everything set 
to air tomorrow will miss deadline!

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:42.090
Yeah, almost all.

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:43.620
Almost all...

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:45.090
Don't they produce any episodes in advance?

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:47.920
Almost none of them.

00:10:47.420 --> 00:10:49.310
What are we going to do?

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:52.220
Please, leave it to us.

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:53.500
Who are you people?

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:10.720
<b>Six</b>

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:10.720
<b>Five</b>

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:10.720
<b>Three</b>

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:10.720
<b>Two</b>

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:10.720
<b>Four</b>

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:03.000
We deliver milk to the city every day.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:05.920
But in reality, we're anime contractors.

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:07.740
I've heard of this organization...

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:10.730
When a studio is about to miss its 
submission deadline, they appear

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:15.400
and invoice astronomical amounts 
just to get one episode made.

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:17.360
What an unfair accusation.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:23.200
We merely charge an appropriate 
fee for keeping production alive.

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:26.420
So, what did you people come here for?

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:30.740
I know a way to stop 
Chizilla in its tracks...

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:33.200
and I'm offering it to you.

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:49.020
<b>Okinawa Soba</b>

00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:47.080
Okinawa soba is delicious!

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:48.480
Juicy, too!

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:53.340
The massive creature Chizilla, 
following the will of Mr. Chiba,

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:54.640
is currently dormant.

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:58.240
It discharged all of its stored 
energy on Sagami-OHno.

00:11:54.650 --> 00:12:00.650
<b>Chizilla Disaster Planning Headquarters
Special Conference Room 202</b>

00:11:58.240 --> 00:11:59.600
I believe you know what happened next.

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:00.640
Of course.

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:05.190
If it's doing what Mr. Chiba would have 
done, its final destination will be Suginami.

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:07.280
<b>Two</b>

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:07.280
He would have no 
reason to burn that city.

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:08.920
That's correct.

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:12.120
Why did Chizilla discharge 
all his energy there?

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:14.270
<b>Sugami-OHno</b>

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:17.120
Isn't it just that Sagami-OHno was on a 
direct line from MiyageSAY Lake to Suginami?

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:19.880
<b>Suginami</b>

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:19.630
The bridge is along that course, too.

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:21.130
<b>Sagami-OHno</b>

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:25.840
<b>Two</b>

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:25.840
<b>Three</b>

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:24.740
We've analyzed Mr. Chiba's PC.

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:27.870
It contained a staffer blacklist.

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:30.610
There was one particular 
problem child among them.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:40.730
<b>April 24 Comichiya
Stop at all costs!!</b>

00:12:30.610 --> 00:12:32.630
Of all things, that staff member...

00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:37.060
...wrote that he was going to a doujinshi 
trade show right before deadline.

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:39.240
Then, near that, in Mr. 
Chiba's handwriting...

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:40.740
...is a note reading "Stop at all costs!"

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:44.960
So his desire to stop the staff member from 
going to that doujinshi trade show...

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:46.700
...reduced a city to cinders.

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:48.880
Why did they even hire that guy?

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:56.250
<b>Two</b>

00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:51.610
In an industry plagued by 
chronic understaffing issues,

00:12:51.610 --> 00:12:54.370
you can't not hire someone just 
because they're "difficult."

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:56.250
<b>Three</b>

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:56.250
Please, listen to this.

00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:59.570
<i>I'd rather die than miss 
the doujinshi trade show!</i>

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:06.470
<b>I'd rather die!!</b>

00:13:00.010 --> 00:13:03.690
<i>I'd rather die than miss 
the doujinshi trade show!</i>

00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:06.460
No wonder he discharged his energy...

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:08.390
Back to the subject at hand.

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:11.670
Chizilla's motivations are extremely 
close to those of Mr. Chiba.

00:13:11.670 --> 00:13:13.990
Thus, to stop—or rather, 
reassure—Mr. Chiba,

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:16.120
32 Years Old 
Blood Type AB

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:18.030
the best measure would be to deliver 
the episode he was tasked to complete.

00:13:19.100 --> 00:13:22.610
And you're overseeing 
production of that episode?

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:23.860
Yes, indeed.

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:23.860
<b>Two</b>

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:25.120
What's the deadline?

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:26.740
<b>Three</b>

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:26.740
Three days from now.

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:29.220
How much time until Chizilla 
begins to move again?

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:32.010
According to calculations of the rate 
he's accumulating heat energy...

00:13:32.010 --> 00:13:33.530
likely 72 hours from now.

00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:35.530
Almost the same time.

00:13:35.530 --> 00:13:38.010
So if we can get the episode 
delivered before he awakens,

00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:41.050
Chizilla will be satisfied 
and stop his rampage?

00:13:41.330 --> 00:13:46.220
It's merely a hypothesis, but that 
seems the most likely scenario.

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:50.800
Well? Can you make the deadline?

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:52.730
We were on schedule until yesterday.

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:53.800
However...

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:55.300
However?

00:13:55.550 --> 00:13:59.000
Yesterday, the production committee 
decided to scrap everything—

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:00.570
storyboards included—and start over.

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:01.910
Come on!

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:03.450
What will we do?

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:05.140
You can't argue with the production committee!

00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:05.650
That is why...

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:16.660
<b>Four      Three      Two</b>

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:08.330
In order to deliver the episode safely,

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:12.900
we request that the government 
put out a strong statement

00:14:12.900 --> 00:14:16.670
asking the entire anime industry 
to be on standby to assist us.

00:14:17.530 --> 00:14:18.910
Very well.

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:20.660
And... here.

00:14:24.810 --> 00:14:26.640
You're taking advantage of us.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:33.140
<b>Four</b>

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:33.140
<b>Three</b>

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:33.140
<b>Two</b>

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:29.280
Surely it's a small price to 
pay to prevent the destruction

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:32.830
of Suginami and ensure the continued
existence of the anime industry.

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:36.770
<b>5RS 
Extravagant Special Production Room</b>

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:41.400
That was easier than I thought it'd be.

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:44.350
With a budget like this, 
we might just make it.

00:14:44.350 --> 00:14:46.740
Or we could say, "Screw you, got ours."

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:49.200
If we did that, they'd run 
us out of the country.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.300
Then we'll live abroad!

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:50.990
Acceptable!

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:53.060
<i>Not</i> acceptable!

00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:55.940
We are cyborgs, built to 
serve the greater good.

00:14:55.940 --> 00:14:58.850
We throw caution to the wind. 
We run to the aid of others.

00:14:58.850 --> 00:15:01.240
That is who we are. That is our justice!

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:07.510
Five

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:07.510
Three

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:07.510
Two

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:07.510
Four

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:07.510
Six

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:05.370
Storyboards and design 
materials are complete.

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:06.810
We have 70 hours left.

00:15:06.810 --> 00:15:07.500
Let's do it.

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:08.630
<b>Two</b>

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:08.620
Yes!

00:15:08.930 --> 00:15:09.640
Right!

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:10.630
<b>Four</b>

00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:10.620
Yeah!

00:15:10.620 --> 00:15:11.630
Heh!

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:11.640
<b>Five</b>

00:15:11.630 --> 00:15:13.260
Let's get it done!

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:13.640
<b>Six</b>

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:20.140
Five

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:20.140
Three

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:20.140
Two

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:20.140
Four

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:20.140
Six

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:20.140
<i>A special envoy from a certain 
country is requesting a meeting.</i>

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:21.350
<b>5RS</b>

00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:27.430
Congress has decided on a 
full-scale attack on Chizilla.

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:27.440
<b>5RS Meeting Room
(Not completed in time for reforms)</b>

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:36.200
<b>Special Envoy Shiva Ayano</b>

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:29.740
What are you talking about?

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:32.790
The plan to stop Chizilla 
is proceeding smoothly!

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:36.210
I've analyzed production 
schedules in your industry.

00:15:36.850 --> 00:15:38.840
You claim you can make the deadline?

00:15:38.840 --> 00:15:40.460
Almost assuredly.

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:59.430
<b>Deadline Over All</b>

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:44.670
You say that, but you Japanese 
frequently break your promises...

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:47.950
Our staff won't break its promises.

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:50.940
Can't you postpone the operation?

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:52.600
No.

00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:56.260
Our current leader is like a raging bull.

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:58.480
There's no stopping it.

00:15:58.480 --> 00:15:59.420
But...

00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:01.900
The bull makes the decisions for us.

00:16:02.710 --> 00:16:05.430
Who makes the decisions for your show?

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:08.700
Saying that will cause a lot of problems...

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:12.450
<b>Deadline Over All</b>

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:11.610
Indeed.

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:13.940
We really need your help.

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:13.950
Health issues (off)
On the train!
On the train
Home briefly, back noon

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:13.950
