00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:16.590
<b>Also, staff working from home</b>

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:19.170
150 animation directors, 
each with a quota of two cuts.

00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:23.180
With 150 animation directors, there'll 
be no consistency in the animation.

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:24.560
What's the point of having them?

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:26.750
Apparently it's the creator's will.

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:28.870
They told us to have animation 
directors, no matter what.

00:17:29.590 --> 00:17:31.420
There's no point!

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:31.690
<b>Opinions are their own.</b>

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:31.980
<b>Five</b>

00:17:29.710 --> 00:17:31.980
<b>Three</b>

00:17:29.750 --> 00:17:31.980
<b>Four</b>

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:35.310
The moment the keyframes 
are done, we'll scan them,

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:35.320
<b>Do Not Use Feeder</b>

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:39.340
and send them to in-between and 
coloring studios all over the country.

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:41.440
Then what?

00:17:42.070 --> 00:17:43.750
Everything up to key animation will make it.

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:44.460
<b>In-Between Office</b>

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:47.450
But we're sorely lacking in domestic studios 
to handle in-betweening and coloring.

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:47.460
<b>Finishing Room</b>

00:17:47.450 --> 00:17:49.460
What?!

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:51.580
Delays in training new staff 
have trapped us even here?

00:17:51.580 --> 00:17:54.200
Instead of dealing with the 
per-frame price cut problem...

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:56.280
We've become completely 
reliant on foreign outsourcing!

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:58.590
<b>Five</b>

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:58.600
Using the lack of a schedule as an 
excuse not to make any reforms...

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:01.850
<b>Six</b>

00:17:58.600 --> 00:18:01.840
To think the warping of the industry 
structure could be our fatal undoing!

